<title>USA: White House to review tobacco deal for several weeks.</title>
<headline>White House to review tobacco deal for several weeks.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton said on Friday that the federal government would study an agreement between U.S. states and the tobacco industry for several weeks to see whether it was in the best interests of public health.</p>
<p>&quot;Until now, we have not had the opportunity to review the actual terms of the agreement and we have not concluded whether it is in the best interests of public health,&quot; Clinton said in a statement. &quot;Over the next several weeks, we will undertake a thorough public health review.&quot;</p>
</text>
